WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.848
Hannah: The compatibility matrix covers our production interpreter. Authentication refresh, pagination, and timeout paths pass.

2
00:00:10.848 --> 00:00:18.408
Raj: The supported release changes timeout exception types. I updated our explicit handling and tests.

3
00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:25.055
Lukas: Did the tests use real response shapes? Simplified mocks can hide pagination changes.

4
00:00:25.055 --> 00:00:33.911
Anika: Yes, sanitized captured responses and contract fixtures. Just to confirm, no production tokens, right?

5
00:00:33.911 --> 00:00:41.327
Hannah: Correct, credentials come from the test tenant. The smoke test checks the complete sync.

6
00:00:41.327 --> 00:00:49.799
Priya: Okay, install using hash-locked requirements every time. We need the tested combination, not something similar.

7
00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:57.191
Lukas: Check connection cleanup after cancelled requests too. Success paths won't expose leaked resources.

8
00:00:57.191 --> 00:01:04.318
Raj: The cancellation tests now release their connections. We can rule that out in covered cases.

9
00:01:04.318 --> 00:01:11.422
Anika: Maybe large inventories still behave differently here. I'll add a representative multi-page dataset.

10
00:01:11.422 --> 00:01:19.630
Priya: Agreed, keep untested combinations clearly excluded. Approval covers this interpreter and platform only.

